WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.440
Do you remember Mary Lil Fargo,
Elder Brother?

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.360
The only daughter of the Fargo Family,
a branch family of the Animusphere Family,

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.240
which is in charge
of the Astromancy Department.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.700
She used to be my student.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.530
What about her?

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.910
Earlier, a messenger
from the Animusphere Family came over.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.620
She said Mary's father,
Ernest Fargo, had suddenly died.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.380
Not only dead, but his body
was dismembered in his own home.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.840
Quite a few Mages
have already thrown in the towel,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.340
so she insisted on consulting
the Lord of Modern Magecraft Theories.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.180
There's one thing I'd like to ask.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.560
Why do I have to get involved in this case?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.350
Oh, that's an easy one.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.610
All first-class Mages
are wealthy except for you.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.990
So naturally, his considerable inheritance
will fall right into Mary's lap.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.070
If it works out,
you can expect a generous reward.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.330
Maybe you could put a dent
in that debt of yours.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.790
Pain in the neck...

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.080
Come on, the least you can do
is muster some enthusiasm

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.500
for taking revenge on the killer
of your student's father, Elder Brother.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.920
I'm not a superhero.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.180
And I've never wanted to become one.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
Gray...

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.100
Can I rely on you?

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:21.970
Yes.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:56.070
THE FARGO MANSION, ENGLAND

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.070
A rotunda...

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:05.740
What's that, sir?

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.120
A building with a dome-like roof like that.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.500
The roof refers to the sky

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.290
while the inside symbolizes Earth.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:16.800
In other words, the whole building
represents the world.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.170
One can say that the master of the house
is the god of that world for a time.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.430
God of that world...

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.850
Even with such an obvious clue
before them, why couldn't they solve it?

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.220
Sir?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.850
Never mind.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:30.980
Let's go.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.560
I am in charge of taking care
of this mansion.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.270
The name is Claire, the maid.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.150
Miss,

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.030
Lord El-Melloi is here to see you.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:45.990
Sir!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.120
Thank you so much for coming!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.700
I don't know what to do!

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.670
Don't be pathetic.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:54.330
Remember what I taught you?

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:58.420
A Mage must keep a level head
especially in times of trouble.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:03.050
Who's this?

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.840
She's Gray. My apprentice.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:08.310
Forgive the impoliteness
of having her hood on.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.100
Now then, share with me
the details of the incident.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.350
I shall explain that.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.560
And you are...

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.780
It's an honor to meet you, Lord El-Melloi.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.360
I am Fernando Li, Ernest's friend
and fellow researcher.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.660
I am a Spiritual Evocationist.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.170
Then, why don't you use Spiritual Evocation
to question the victim?

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.790
I knew it wouldn't work, but I did try.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.500
Unfortunately, there's
a bounded field in the mansion.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.260
I wouldn't trust this guy if I were you.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:45.720
Alec!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.100
After all, he may be the one
who murdered Uncle Ernest.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:53.100
Alec! How could you say that to Fernando?

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.230
Are you Mr. Fargo's nephew Alec?

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.310
I'm flattered!

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.610
You know about a dropout Mage like me?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.240
Do you think I'm suspicious?

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:05.950
When it comes to Mages,

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:10.740
fellow researchers are no different than
assassins who'd kill you in your sleep, right?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.200
True.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.670
But I heard that you owe
great sums of money to Ernest.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.500
Yes.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.460
On the day of the incident,

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.470
Alec was arguing
with the master about that.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.470
Claire, you wench!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.590
Alec, stop it!

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.930
Claire, that's enough from you, too.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:35.680
You have no right
to say anything on this matter.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.810
I apologize, Miss.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.690
Were you here
the night Ernest Fargo died?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.440
Yes. Of course.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:48.070
Just four of us were here that night.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.570
I see.

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:54.410
Now, I'd like to see the site
of Ernest Fargo's death.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.790
The report said parts of Mr. Fargo's body
were found in five spots in here,

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.250
and also in two spots
elsewhere in the mansion,

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.130
for a total of seven spots.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.510
The structure of this passage suits
Magecraft that uses celestial bodies.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:14.010
I suppose the seven planets.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.020
The seven planets?

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:22.820
I recall from your class that the seven planets
correspond to parts of the human body.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:23.820
That's right.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.820
And by looking at how the parts
were placed,

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:31.700
it should become clear who used them
for Magecraft and for what motive.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.710
Is that all the infamous Lord has to offer?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.460
Even an infant Mage
can figure out that much.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.670
If things were that simple,

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.800
I wouldn't have bothered
the main family to call you here.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:54.010
We used our Magecraft
to preserve the crime scene.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:56.180
I'll take a look.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:12.620
This is...

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:14.700
Now you understand what we said, Lord?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.830
I do.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.120
I don't blame you
for being at a loss here.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.960
As a branch of the Animusphere Family,

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.340
we are Astromancers.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.300
Everything you've said so far
is the first thing we thought of.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.720
The way the parts are lined up
doesn't apply to the traditions we know.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.180
It's Modern Magecraft.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:38.970
So, you thought if it is Modern Magecraft,
I might be able to solve this?

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:39.930
Indeed.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.480
I will do what I can.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.610
Please, sir.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.490
This building...

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.990
It feels suffocating.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.200
It's kind of like a cage.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:01.040
Lady, a "cage" is the perfect descriptor for it.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:05.080
Sir, is one of them the murderer?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.130
They said a bounded field was placed
in the mansion on the day of the murder.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.590
It's hard to think
that an outside intruder did this.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.680
For Fernando, it would be
about Mr. Fargo's research results.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.180
For Alec, his fortune.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.390
They both have a motive.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:23.520
And with her father dead,
Mary could inherit both of those things.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.110
What? Do you suspect Mary, too, sir?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.530
I'm just talking about possibilities, Lady.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.280
Then, those three are suspects?

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.360
No, there's actually one more person.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.950
You don't mean Claire, the maid?

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.700
But she's not a Mage, is she?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.710
The majority of mutilation murders
all over the world

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.960
are carried out
by people who aren't Mages.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:52.090
I'm not certain, but I believe
Claire was physically abused by Mr. Fargo.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:54.840
Physically abused...

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:57.390
Her sudden movements were slow.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.720
It's the movement of a person
with injuries under their clothing.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.350
Long clothing to hide the bruises of abuse.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.350
That's terrible.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.350
Do you think Mary knew it?

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.980
She may have.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.230
But that doesn't mean she could stop it.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.820
Why not?

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.200
To a Mage, one's children are property.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.240
She wouldn't have dared defy her father.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:28.290
Who knows what repulsive secrets
lie in a Mage's home?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:31.300
I can't say with any certainty
that Mary has no motive.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.050
Then, all four of them have a motive.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:40.720
Yes. Mages bring about unpredictable
supernatural phenomena.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:41.810
Therefore,

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.310
howdunit.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:46.810
How was it done?
There's no room for conjecture.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.320
But the whydunit...
Why did they do it? That's different.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.820
Yes, that's the key to solve the mystery.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.330
At any rate, it seems
we don't have enough information yet.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.040
I'm going for a walk.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.580
Wait up!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.120
I'm going with you!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:13.050
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝ Grace note

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.090
Yes. He was perfectly healthy.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.590
He was a heavy smoker,

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.720
but very youthful for his age.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.230
And my father often said,

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:32.480
"Life is too short to reach the Root."

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.740
Reaching the Root
is the dream of every Mage.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:41.370
That's why Mages inherit a Magical Crest

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:44.240
and entrust that dream
to the next generation.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:49.000
To the end, my father thought
he wanted to reach the Root.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.290
So it couldn't have been suicide!

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.710
I see.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:57.260
So, was Ernest's research related to that?

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.380
Yes. As far as I can remember,

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.640
my father would often say the word "eternal."

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.470
"Eternal"?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.060
He was searching for the everlasting.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:14.570
That's what I believed in
for the longest time without any doubts...

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.400
until I met you.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:17.900
Me?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.570
In ancient times, people thought
the planets were immutable.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.330
But now we know that isn't so.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.870
As you know, even the geocentric model,

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:31.670
the premise that Astromancy is based on,

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.960
was overturned in the 17th century. Therefore...

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.470
- Even the twinkling of the stars isn't forever.
- Even the twinkling of the stars isn't forever.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.220
That's my teacher.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:44.390
Well,

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.470
I'm impressed you remember
what I said in class.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.810
Even then, you were an excellent student.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.440
I've had my eye on these for a while.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:59.360
Rare Magecraft tomes
should net me a fortune.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.660
Searching for a culprit, my ass.
What nonsense.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.620
I should be able to get
all the pieces soon, but...

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.420
Sir, something's been bothering me.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.790
What's the problem with the hall?

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.050
Oh, right.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.670
I'll lay it out for you.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.720
As I've also explained in class,

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:28.100
the parts of the human body
correspond to the seven planets.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:28.760
Yes.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:29.930
For example,

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.480
Mars with the head,

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.810
Mercury with the chest and arms,

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.690
and the Sun with the heart.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:40.530
The head, trunk, head, arms
and heart were in the hall.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:44.410
The bones and hair were in the library.
The legs were in storage.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.910
Certainly, you said the way
they were lined up didn't match the theory.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.200
Correct.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.660
What nailed it was the heart,
associated with the Sun,

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.960
placed in the center of the room.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.380
If the Sun is in the center,
it doesn't work?

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.010
With this type of Magecraft,

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.970
the Mage is in the center of the room,

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:07.970
and around them are placed the items
which carry out the functions of the Code.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.350
However, here,

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.930
the heart was placed in the center of the room.

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.820
It's like the corpse itself used Magecraft!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.370
Is something wrong, sir?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.250
Lord, come quick!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.210
Alec! Why?

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:45.720
This is how I found him.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.300
A second murder case, huh?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:51.060
This is like a third-rate mystery.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:55.270
Hey, I smell something!

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:58.060
Who said that?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.070
If Add reacted to something...

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.150
Yes.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:06.030
Traces of the undead are still here.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.400
Undead, you say?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.660
The bones and hair are symbols of Saturn

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:13.290
which rules over the domain of the dead.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:18.040
Residue of the Saturn Mana
summoned the undead.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:19.750
Necromancy.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.670
That's your specialty, isn't it?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.170
Ridiculous!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.470
Are you saying I summoned the undead?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:31.390
No. But your research
is definitely being applied.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.390
Mine?

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:37.310
Let's go to the central hall.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:42.110
I'll disclose everything there.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.280
Well?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.360
Sir,

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.610
who is the murderer?

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.120
I'll explain everything in order.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:59.620
First, the Magecraft set up in this mansion
was indeed Seven Planets.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.460
That's why the body was split up
and placed in seven locations.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.420
Now, wait just a minute!

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.050
We already said that was impossible!

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.380
That was a trap.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.510
A trap?

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.390
When your family, an offshoot
of the Animusphere Family,

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.020
uses Astromancy, you follow
the geocentric model, right?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.520
That's correct.

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.360
Magecraft that follows the heliocentric theory,
in which Earth is not at the center,

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.280
is no more than a technique
with a short history!

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.780
It goes against our traditions!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.070
Yes. That's the Animusphere aesthetic.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.290
But there was someone
who abandoned that belief.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.540
It was Ernest Fargo himself.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.620
What?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.750
He wanted to pursue something...

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.050
even if he had to twist things
like tradition, aesthetics, faith.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.260
That something was his dream
he wanted to realize.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.140
As I thought.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.480
Th-That's...

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:08.190
The heart, which symbolizes the Sun,
was placed in the center of the mansion.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.570
Then, in a circular pattern,
come the arms of Mercury,

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:12.990
and continuing with the throat of Venus.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:17.030
The Sun, Mercury, Venus and next...

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.450
Earth?

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.910
Yes.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.540
But there is no body part
that corresponds with Earth.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.710
The soul corresponds with it.

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:30.510
So, I thought something here
must contain his soul.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:52.030
As I suspected,
the mansion itself is a workshop

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:55.160
designed to give you eternal existence!

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.330
Father!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:03.410
Mary, my daughter...

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.380
Give me your life!

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.920
I don't have enough yet for eternity!

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.380
Life...

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.970
Knowledge...

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.930
Power!

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:19.310
Hey!

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:21.020
This guy's bad news!

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:22.850
Father...

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.310
Why?

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.190
The ritual was imperfect.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.480
It was a spell
at the experimental level,

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:30.520
something new
to your family's tradition.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.320
Naturally, it wouldn't be stable.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.530
On top of that,

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:35.320
he wasn't merely aiming
for life extension,

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:36.820
but immortality!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.200
Ernest!

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:43.370
Instead of entrusting his dream
to the next generation like other Mages,

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:47.210
he wanted to reach the Root
himself at any cost.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:49.630
So, using the heavens
and Earth as his model,

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.750
he scattered pieces of his own body,

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:55.590
which symbolized the seven planets,
inside this mansion, a microcosm of the world.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.260
What have you done?

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:01.310
By doing that, he intended to become one
with the cosmos of this mansion,

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:03.890
thereby achieving an eternal existence!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.150
My dream...

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:10.980
Root...

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.650
Beyond this world!

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.660
Sir, I think it's too late to...

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:21.910
I know.

00:18:23.740 --> 00:18:25.410
Can you do it, Gray?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.500
Yes.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:31.210
H-Hey, what are you...

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:32.800
By herself? It's too dangerous!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.460
We should back her up!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.460
Unnecessary.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:37.090
In fact, we should move back.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.470
Otherwise, we'll get caught in the middle!

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:40.850
Add!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:41.680
On it!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.640
<i>First stage restraint rescinded!</i>

00:18:58.490 --> 00:18:59.360
That's...

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:03.870
Could it be an Anti-Undead Mystic Code?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.040
I love it! A buffet!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.300
<i>Gray.</i>

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:15.840
<i>Rave.</i>

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:17.800
<i>Crave.</i>

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.180
<i>Deprave.</i>

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.520
She's preying on the Mana all around her?

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.350
Sir, what on earth is your apprentice?

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.770
You think I'll just let you destroy me?

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:40.780
I am eternal!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.120
<i>Grave me.</i>

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.460
<i>Grave for you.</i>

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.700
It's all right now.

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.080
Just leave the rest to the main family.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.120
Thank you for everything.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:36.090
I didn't do much.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:41.420
Still, I can't believe he ventured
to test such incomplete Magecraft.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:46.100
It was always my father's dearest wish
to attain immortality.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:51.350
Well, there's one deduction I made
that I didn't share in there.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.270
Sir?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.100
Mary, you knew, didn't you?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.520
That your father's ritual
would end in failure.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.240
You're an outstanding Mage.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.410
Even if he didn't tell you the whole story,

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:09.580
I'm sure you had many means to learn
the nature of his research and objective.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.580
Of course, you didn't have
murderous intent.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:18.840
But you didn't stop your father
from engaging in a faulty ritual, either.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.050
Am I wrong?

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:24.510
If you're right, what then?

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.720
Nothing. There's nothing I can do.

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:29.890
I don't have any proof.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.850
It's just a hypothesis.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:34.310
But the whydunit?

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:37.270
I'm a bit curious why you didn't stop him.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.150
If my father achieved his immortality,

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:45.530
my situation would never change.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:50.530
My father would've kept me captive
in this cage of a mansion for the rest of my life.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:55.410
So, all I did was prove to him
that nothing was eternal.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.790
Just as you taught me.

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:05.170
Thank you, sir. Thank you so much.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:06.930
Take care.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:17.100
Nothing is eternal.

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:19.270
Everything changes.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.860
And people are no exception.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:23.190
Sir...

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.700
Let's go home.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.910
Yes, sir.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:40.080
EPISODE 2: The Seven Stars and the Eternal Cage
